Z||000001||Black88GT||04-09-2001||04:30 PM||||Paint is gonna be expensive.  I am expecting around $1500 when I am ready for mine and thats just black paint.  I would take mine to my friends Dads shop in Frederick, MD.  He does good work there and since I know him there is less of a chance of getting ripped.  <P>I do remember on the MAFOA mailing list someone worked at a body shop and quoted me around $2,000.  You might want to ask them, not sure if you belong to MAFOA, but I could ask them for you if not.<P>How about this weather?  I had my t-tops off for the first time.  Almost forgot how much I loved that exhaust tone...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">  <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I>||||reg||6
